# Template for secrets.bndrun, which is deliberately NOT in git (see .gitignore next to this
# file). Copy it, fill in the tokens, and launch.bndrun picks them up through the optional
# `-include: -secrets.bndrun`:
#
#     cp secrets.bndrun.template secrets.bndrun
#
# The mechanism is the same as in org.eclipse.fennec.mcp.emf.runtime: values arrive as system
# properties and are read from the Configurator JSON as
# $[env:NAME;default=$[prop:NAME;default=…]], resolved by
# org.apache.felix.configadmin.plugin.interpolation. An exported environment variable wins
# over this file; a value left out falls back to the empty default, which keeps the shipped
# behaviour - no token, direct loopback callers only.
#
# MCP_INFERENCE_AUTH_TOKEN guards /mcp/inference (HttpMCPServerComponent~inference in
# …mcp.inference.config), the only endpoint this runtime serves - the task-scoped set for
# inferring a metamodel and publishing it to the model atlas. This is the endpoint event.atlas
# calls: the value must match METAMODEL_MCP_TOKEN in that repo's own secrets.bndrun, alongside
# a METAMODEL_MCP_URL pointing at this servlet's public tunnel.
#
# /mcp/emf is NOT served here - it belongs to org.eclipse.fennec.mcp.emf.runtime, which has its
# own secrets.bndrun and its own MCP_EMF_AUTH_TOKEN.
#
# Remember that the filter refuses a loopback request carrying an X-Forwarded-For / Forwarded
# header - the shape any tunnel (ngrok, cloudflared) produces - so exposing an endpoint and
# setting its token are one step, not two.
# The three MODEL_ATLAS_* / MCP_ATLAS_* values configure ModelAtlasPublisher~publisher, which
# ships in org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.mcp.config. base.uri and scope have no usable
# default and are validated at activation: leave either blank and the publisher refuses to
# activate, post_to_model_atlas is not published, and MCPToolProvider~inference stays one tool
# short of its minimum. stage may be omitted - it defaults to 'draft', and it should stay a
# draft stage.
#
# MCP_ATLAS_PUBLISH_ALLOWLIST is a '|'-separated list of namespace URIs, each either exact or a
# prefix ending in '*'. Deny-all: a namespace no rule admits cannot be published, and neither
# scope nor stage nor overwrite is ever a tool parameter. The separator is a pipe and NOT a
# comma because bnd splits -runvm on commas - a comma-separated value would arrive as a
# truncated list plus a stray JVM argument. Use '\|' for a pipe inside a rule.
#
#     -DMCP_ATLAS_PUBLISH_ALLOWLIST=https://eclipse.org/fennec/lorawan/*|https://fennec.eclipse.org/event.atlas/inferred*
#
# An exported environment variable of the same name wins over anything set here.
-runvm.secrets: \
	-DMCP_INFERENCE_AUTH_TOKEN=REPLACE-ME,\
	-DMODEL_ATLAS_BASE_URI=REPLACE-ME,\
	-DMODEL_ATLAS_PUBLISHING_SCOPE=REPLACE-ME,\
	-DMCP_ATLAS_PUBLISH_ALLOWLIST=REPLACE-ME

